<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (The experimental results demonstrate that transformer-based models provide a significant performance advantage for short-text classification, with BERT achieving the highest Macro F1-score of 0.9481. Its strong contextual understanding enables accurate topic prediction even when input text is brief or lacks explicit detail. In contrast, classical and recurrent models struggled with ambiguous or overlapping content.)
/Pg 21 0 R
>>
endobj
251 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (Overall, the findings confirm that BERT is highly effective for tweet-like topic classification tasks and can serve as a robust foundation for applications such as real-time social media monitoring, automated news categorization, and trend analysis. Future work may explore the use of actual Twitter datasets, domain-specific pretraining, or more advanced transformer architectures such as RoBERTa or DeBERTa to further improve performance.)
/Pg 21 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
